WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:03.381
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:04.232 --> 00:00:05.460
- All right.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.990
Oh my gosh. I love seeing the rink.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.180
That was so cool with the
Kelly Clarkson Show on it.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.160
We're very fancy here at 30 Rock.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.200
Band, you are sounding incredible today.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.136
Give it up for the band.

00:00:14.136 --> 00:00:15.995
(crowd cheering)

00:00:15.995 --> 00:00:17.280
Well, everybody, we've got time

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.500
for one more story I
discovered on social media.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.723
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:23.340
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.890
I think we all sat in disbelief
seeing the devastation

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.990
in Maui after the fires this summer.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.310
It's one of those moments when you think

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.450
what can I do to help?

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.680
And that's exactly what went

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.870
through five-year-old Edison's mind.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.290
His solution? A lemonade
stand, which is incredible.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.640
So with the help of his parents

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.920
he whipped up yellow and pink lemonade,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.590
set up a table and posted a vibrant sign.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:47.795
And in one day he
raised, get this, $20,000

00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:48.628
(crowd applauding)

00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:49.461
for the Maui Relief Fund.

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.153
Lemonade is powerful.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.560
Beyonce knew. She knew!

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.630
We have Edison and his mom Amy

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.520
on the line right now watching from home

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.650
on KOMO 4 in Seattle.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.530
What's up Edison? What's up mama?

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.210
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.880
- Oh my gosh. So Amy,
how did this all start?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.330
- Yeah, so we took Edison
to Lahaina back in January.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.670
So when we were watching
the news about the fires

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.880
he knew what, where we were talking about.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.890
He remembered our trip there

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.720
and I think he felt really sad hearing

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.290
about the kids and parents
who had lost so much.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.080
And so we were on a walk
one night as a family

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.240
and he said, maybe we
can have a lemonade stand

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.734
and I can give all my money
to the people in Lahaina.

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:35.760
And my husband and I looked at each other

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.490
and we thought, how can we,
we have to make that happen.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.380
That's such a cool idea.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.470
And so he sat all day out on a Saturday

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.210
and raised a lot of money.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.680
Everything was listed at one dollar

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.480
but everyone gave a lot more than that.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.670
- I noticed from the twenty grand. Yeah.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.070
I was like, that is good lemonade.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.980
You should open an
establishment at that point.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.510
Well, Edison, how does it make you feel

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.270
to help these people that needed the help?

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.840
- Happy and proud

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.103
because I helped everyone.

00:02:06.103 --> 00:02:08.160
- Absolutely the best feeling too.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.260
Being happy, helping
others makes you happy.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.580
I think we forget that sometimes.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.220
Thank you for reminding us Edison.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.410
You guys, y'all are amazing
and thank you so much.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.750
Amy and Edison, I'm liking
your post right now, Okay?

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.400
- [Edison] Yeah.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.390
- He's so cute.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:22.223
Well, that's not all.

00:02:22.223 --> 00:02:24.720
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.030
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.010
want to celebrate your kind heart

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.860
so they're giving the Maui
Strong Fund a thousand dollars

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.825
to help even more people in Lahaina.

00:02:33.825 --> 00:02:37.050
(crowd cheering)

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.660
Thank you guys so much.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.130
Congrats on your lemonade stand

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.810
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.207
Leslie Odom Jr., Mike Birbiglia,

00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:48.600
Jackie, Matt and Bryan
from The Awesome Company.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.609
Y'all have a great day.

00:02:49.609 --> 00:02:50.692
(crowd cheering)

